    "body": "tox_pass_key_derive_with_salt's salt was documented as \"at least TOX_PASS_SALT_LENGTH\" bytes; it is exactly that size.\n\n<!-- Reviewable:start -->\n- - -\nThis change is [<img src=\"https://reviewable.io/review_button.svg\" height=\"34\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"Reviewable\"/>](https://reviewable.io/reviews/TokTok/c-toxcore/3044)\n<!-- Reviewable:end -->\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": "2026-05-19T15:29:40Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The reason this was \"at least\" is because anything less than that will cause a buffer overflow. You can still pass it a buffer larger than that size with no effect one way or another. ",
